From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tompta1 <546706+tompta1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:31:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: aop: Stay bound when the firmware cannot be
 halted

When probe fails after the firmware started and it then cannot be
halted, the driver keeps the firmware's memory but returns the error, so
the device is unbound and its devm state (the RTKit instance, mailbox and
DMA buffers the running firmware still uses) is freed under it. Stay
bound, marked as removing, until reboot instead. This only changes the
failure path, on every board with an AOP.

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf), split out of
 kernel/patches/drivers/soc-apple/0034.]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/apple/aop.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c
index d54ff59b2..72a7dc112 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c
@@ -1104,7 +1104,11 @@ static int apple_aop_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		apple_rtkit_free(aop->rtk);
 		apple_aop_free_buffers(aop);
 	} else {
-		dev_err(dev, "failed to halt; keeping its memory\n");
+		/* RTKit still refers to the devm state: retain the bound device too. */
+		aop->removing = true;
+		platform_set_drvdata(pdev, aop);
+		dev_crit(dev, "failed to halt; retaining bound device until reboot\n");
+		return 0;
 	}
 	return ret;
 
